From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nerves TicWatch Pro 3 maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: qup: support SPI_NO_CS mode

SPI_NO_CS is implemented by the SPI core: it suppresses calls to the
controller's chip-select operation.  Advertising the flag therefore needs no
QUP register programming, and permits devices such as Mobvoi's STM32 nanohub
to drive a separately described GPIO chip select with protocol-specific
timing.

Signed-off-by: Nerves TicWatch Pro 3 maintainers <noreply@example.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-qup.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c b/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
@@ -1090,7 +1090,8 @@ static int spi_qup_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	host->use_gpio_descriptors = true;
 	host->max_native_cs = SPI_NUM_CHIPSELECTS;
 	host->bus_num = pdev->id;
-	host->mode_bits = SPI_CPOL | SPI_CPHA | SPI_CS_HIGH | SPI_LOOP;
+	host->mode_bits = SPI_CPOL | SPI_CPHA | SPI_CS_HIGH | SPI_LOOP |
+			  SPI_NO_CS;
 	host->bits_per_word_mask = SPI_BPW_RANGE_MASK(4, 32);
 	host->max_speed_hz = max_freq;
 	host->transfer_one = spi_qup_transfer_one;
-- 
